    "extraction_notes": "Single SoA table in the excerpt (Table 1: Schedule of Events), document pages 17-18. One leading label column (L=1); first data column is position 2; six data columns (2 Screening, 3 Randomization, 4-6 the three eligible HAE attacks, 7 Final Visit/ET). Column boundaries, cell merges and the three horizontal arrows were confirmed from rule-line geometry recovered from a 200 dpi render (vertical rules at 71.3, 309.6, 368.6, 454.9, 530.3, 600.1, 669.2, 720.4 pt); X marks were binned to header-anchored column centres from pdftotext -bbox and agreed with the visual read in every cell. The Randomization cell of the In-clinic / TeleVisit rows is merged VERTICALLY (the horizontal rule between those two rows is absent in that column only), so its single X is emitted on both activity rows; the schema has no vertical-merge field, so no source_range is set on those two cells. The abbreviations block (C1-INH, ECG, eDiary, ET, GA-NRS, HAE, IMP, PGI-C, PGI-S, RTSM, VAS) carries no printed in-grid marker, so per prompt section 6 no abbreviation annotations were emitted."
  },
