    "notes": "main_soa by the section 2 discriminators: rows are procedures performed on subjects, there is no other table in the excerpt to be a continuation/domain/subsidiary of, and this is the protocol's primary anchor grid. The header rows reprint on document page 18 above the single remaining body row (Adverse Event Review), which is a page split of one logical table, so it is extracted as one table spanning pages 17-18 with the reprinted header counted once rather than as a separate continuation table. Header row 1 label is 'Visit'; header row 2 has no label and its property_name is synthesized. Three rows carry a horizontal double-headed arrow instead of X marks: Conventional on-demand treatment washout (columns 4-6), Concomitant Medication Review (columns 2-7) and Adverse Event Review (columns 2-7); each is distributed one entry per covered column with source_range set."
